✅ 1. Meaning of each CSS class

You have this:

<p class="card-text text-muted mb-4">{{ product.description|truncatewords:15 }}</p>

Bootstrap classes:

card-text → Styles text inside a Bootstrap card.

text-muted → Makes the text grey (less visible).

mb-4 → Margin-bottom: 4 (from Bootstrap spacing system).

Bootstrap spacing classes follow this format:
m  = margin
p  = padding
t  = top
b  = bottom
s  = start (left)
e  = end (right)
x  = left & right
y  = top & bottom
1–5 = size


So:

mb-1 → small bottom margin

mb-2 → medium

mb-3 → bigger

mb-4 → even bigger

mb-5 → maximum (largest)

❓ “No way to add more than mb-4?”

Yes you can! Bootstrap supports up to mb-5 by default.

If you want even more space (bigger than 5), you have options:

Option A — Use inline CSS:
<p style="margin-bottom: 60px;">...</p>

Option B — Add your own class:
.mb-6 {
  margin-bottom: 6rem;
}


Then use it:

<p class="card-text text-muted mb-6">...</p>

✅ 2. What does truncatewords:15 mean?

This part is Django template filter:

{{ product.description|truncatewords:15 }}


It means:

➡️ Show only the first 15 words of the description.
➡️ Add "..." at the end automatically.

Example:
If your description is:

"This smartphone has a high-quality camera, strong battery life, and modern design features..."

truncatewords:15 will display only the first 15 words.

Summary
✔ Bootstrap classes:
Class	Meaning
card-text	Styling for text inside a Bootstrap card
text-muted	Makes text grey
mb-4	Bottom margin level 4
✔ Django filter:
Filter	Meaning
truncatewords:15	Cut text after 15 words
✔ You can use larger margin than mb-4

Use mb-5 or create your own class for larger.

1. What is a Bootstrap card?

A Bootstrap card is a ready-made UI component used to display content inside a box with:

Border

Shadow

Padding

Optional image

Title

Text

Buttons

Footer

A card looks like this:

+-----------------------------------+
|   [Image]                         |
|   Product Name                    |
|   Grey text (text-muted)          |
|   Description                     |
|   Price                           |
|   Button                          |
+-----------------------------------+

✔ Bootstrap card example:
<div class="card" style="width: 18rem;">
  <img src="image.jpg" class="card-img-top" alt="...">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h5 class="card-title">Card title</h5>
    <p class="card-text">Some quick example text.</p>
    <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary">Go somewhere</a>
  </div>
</div>


The class card is what makes it a "Bootstrap card."

✅ 2. What is text-muted?

text-muted is not a card.
It is only a text color class that makes the text lighter/grey.

Example:
<p class="text-muted">This text is grey.</p>


So:

card → a box layout component

text-muted → grey text

They are different.

Quick Difference Table
Class	Purpose
card	Creates card layout box
card-body	Inner content area of a card
card-title	Title styling inside card
card-text	Styles paragraph text in a card
text-muted	Makes text grey/light
mb-4	Adds margin-bottom

