✅ Is a Bootstrap card like a container?
✔ They are similar, but not the same.
🟦 Bootstrap Container

A container is used for page layout structure.
It controls page width, alignment, and spacing.

Think of container like:

🟩 A big box that organizes the whole page.

Example:

<div class="container">
    <!-- Page content here -->
</div>

🟧 Bootstrap Card

A card is a small box used to display content, not layout.

Think of card like:

📦 A small item box inside the page
(used for product, profile, article, blog, etc.)

Example:

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5 class="card-title">Product Name</h5>
        <p class="card-text">Short description...</p>
    </div>
</div>

🔥 Simple Analogy

Imagine a supermarket:

🏬 The building → container

Organizes everything inside.

📦 The product boxes → cards

Each product has its own small box.

📝 Visual way to understand
Container (big):
+--------------------------------------------------+
|               container (full page)              |
|                                                  |
|   +------------------+   +------------------+    |
|   |      card        |   |      card        |    |
|   |   product item   |   |  another item    |    |
|   +------------------+   +------------------+    |
|                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+


So:

container = whole layout

card = small content box inside the layout

✔ Example using both
<div class="container mt-4">

    <div class="card" style="width: 18rem;">
        <img src="phone.jpg" class="card-img-top" alt="Phone">
        <div class="card-body">
            <h5 class="card-title">Oppo A57</h5>
            <p class="card-text text-muted">
                {{ product.description|truncatewords:15 }}
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

</div>

